<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isAssociatedWithIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.example.org/meddevice#Incident> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isAssociatedWithIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a device to a reported incident." .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isAssociatedWithIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is associated with incident" .
# 
# http://www.example.org/meddevice#isManufacturedBy
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isManufacturedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isManufacturedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <http://www.example.org/meddevice#manufactures> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isManufacturedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://www.example.org/meddevice#Device> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isManufacturedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.example.org/meddevice#Manufacturer> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isManufacturedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a device to its manufacturer." .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isManufacturedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is manufactured by" .
# 
# http://www.example.org/meddevice#isSubclassifiedUnder
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isSubclassifiedUnder> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isSubclassifiedUnder> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isSubclassifiedUnder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Transitive property expressing that a risk class or device type falls within a higher classification level. Because it is transitive, if A isSubclassifiedUnder B and B isSubclassifiedUnder C, then A isSubclassifiedUnder C." .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#isSubclassifiedUnder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is subclassified under" .
# 
# http://www.example.org/meddevice#manufactures
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#manufactures> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#manufactures> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://www.example.org/meddevice#Manufacturer> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#manufactures> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.example.org/meddevice#Device> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#manufactures> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a manufacturer to the devices it produces." .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#manufactures> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "manufactures" .
# 
# http://www.example.org/meddevice#triggeredBy
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://www.example.org/meddevice#CorrectiveAction> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.example.org/meddevice#Incident> .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a corrective action to the incident that prompted it." .
<http://www.example.org/meddevice#triggeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "triggered by" .
